WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.567 --> 00:00:03.269
I <00:00:00.600><c>do</c><00:00:00.633><c>n</c><00:00:00.667><c>'</c><00:00:00.700><c>t </c><00:00:00.733><c>wa</c><00:00:00.767><c>nt</c><00:00:00.800><c> t</c><00:00:00.834><c>o </c><00:00:00.867><c>se</c><00:00:00.900><c>e.</c>
<00:00:01.000><c>I</c><00:00:01.034><c>'</c><00:00:01.067><c>m </c><00:00:01.100><c>go</c><00:00:01.134><c>in</c><00:00:01.167><c>g </c><00:00:01.201><c>to</c><00:00:01.234><c> t</c><00:00:01.267><c>ur</c><00:00:01.301><c>n </c><00:00:01.334><c>in</c><00:00:01.367><c>to</c><00:00:01.401><c> a</c><00:00:01.434><c> r</c><00:00:01.468><c>oc</c><00:00:01.501><c>k.</c>

00:00:05.238 --> 00:00:08.274
All right, bladesmiths.
Welcome to the kill test.

00:00:10.042 --> 00:00:11.410
Now, in Greek mythology,

00:00:11.443 --> 00:00:13.612
Perseus used his sword
to decapitate Medusa

00:00:13.679 --> 00:00:16.115
and remove her head from her
body to use it as a weapon.

00:00:16.182 --> 00:00:18.317
To that end,
I will take your weapon

00:00:18.384 --> 00:00:20.319
to help me deliver
some killing slashes

00:00:20.353 --> 00:00:22.888
and blows to liberate
her head from her body.

00:00:23.455 --> 00:00:25.124 align:start size:88% position:13%
Robert, you're up first.
You ready for this?

00:00:25.157 --> 00:00:27.193
-Yes, sir.
-Let's do this.

00:00:27.226 --> 00:00:30.062
Going into the testing,
I am concerned about the weight.

00:00:30.129 --> 00:00:32.531
I'm hoping my blade
can do everything

00:00:32.598 --> 00:00:35.168
that Doug wants it to do,
but I'm concerned.

00:01:08.134 --> 00:01:10.970
All right, Robert. Let's talk
about your sword here.

00:01:11.537 --> 00:01:15.675
I like the design that you have
of the Damascus in there.

00:01:15.708 --> 00:01:20.179
But it's so heavy.
It's about 5 pounds over here.

00:01:20.246 --> 00:01:22.348
But the thing is,
it's so forward heavy.

00:01:22.415 --> 00:01:24.516
Most of the weight is up here.
When I'm lifting this,

00:01:24.550 --> 00:01:26.452
I can feel all the stress
right there.

00:01:27.019 --> 00:01:30.656
This is supposed to be meant to
be a single-handed use weapon.

00:01:31.256 --> 00:01:34.160
Now, your edge is plenty sharp.

00:01:34.194 --> 00:01:38.631
It was easy to thrust and cut,
and it will kill.

00:01:40.767 --> 00:01:42.368
All right, Jared. Your turn.
Are you ready, sir?

00:01:42.401 --> 00:01:44.070
-Yes, sir.
-Let's do this.

00:01:44.137 --> 00:01:46.005
With the test, you never really
know what to expect,

00:01:46.072 --> 00:01:47.774
and anything can go wrong.

00:02:12.298 --> 00:02:17.770
All right, Jared. First up,
you nailed the balance on this.

00:02:17.837 --> 00:02:19.438
It's a one-handed swords.

00:02:19.505 --> 00:02:21.574
It's about 3 pounds lighter
than your opponent's.

00:02:21.607 --> 00:02:26.479
Your edge is razor sharp.
Every slash is deep.

00:02:27.012 --> 00:02:29.081
The thrust, no issues at all.

00:02:29.148 --> 00:02:33.286
And most importantly, sir,
it will kill.

00:02:35.888 --> 00:02:39.125
All right, bladesmiths.
Next up is the strength test.

00:02:39.158 --> 00:02:40.693
Release the J. Neily.

00:02:43.729 --> 00:02:45.197
All right, bladesmiths.

00:02:45.264 --> 00:02:46.999
We took Medusa's head
during the kill test.

00:02:47.066 --> 00:02:48.534
Now the kraken
has turned to stone.

00:02:48.601 --> 00:02:50.536
So what I'm going to do
is take your swords

00:02:50.569 --> 00:02:53.640
and beat them mercilessly
into these stone kraken heads.

00:02:54.741 --> 00:02:56.175
It's going to be brutal.

00:02:56.776 --> 00:02:59.278
And, Rob, you're up first.
How are you feeling?

00:02:59.312 --> 00:03:01.247
A little nervous, but I'm ready.

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:03.716
-Let's do it.
-This is the make or break test.

00:03:20.766 --> 00:03:22.367
You okay?

00:03:22.401 --> 00:03:24.204
Yep. Bounced off the glove.
Didn't cut me.

00:03:25.171 --> 00:03:29.175
-Well, that's that.
-My blade breaks.

00:03:29.241 --> 00:03:33.746
My heart breaks, but I am just
so glad that it didn't hurt J.

00:03:35.214 --> 00:03:37.049
Well, a little bit
of a problem here, Rob.

00:03:37.717 --> 00:03:39.852
On the tang,
you can see a black spot,

00:03:39.919 --> 00:03:42.321
so that means you had
a stress fracture there.

00:03:42.388 --> 00:03:44.223
And with the weight
of this sword

00:03:44.256 --> 00:03:46.459
hitting the stone kraken skulls,

00:03:46.525 --> 00:03:48.294
it was enough to allow
that stress fracture

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:50.662
to just continue
all the way across it.

00:03:50.729 --> 00:03:55.034
So the good part
is that your edge held up,

00:03:55.601 --> 00:03:57.570
so good job on the Damascus,

00:03:57.603 --> 00:04:00.506
but it's kind of hard to swing
a sword without a handle on it.

00:04:06.145 --> 00:04:07.547
Well, Robert, your blade

00:04:07.613 --> 00:04:10.616
broke after four strokes
on this kraken head,

00:04:10.683 --> 00:04:12.919
but that doesn't mean that
you're out of the competition.

00:04:12.952 --> 00:04:16.522
Jared, your blade still
has to survive four strikes.

00:04:16.589 --> 00:04:18.258
J, let's get crack-a-lacking.

00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:22.662
This is it right here.

00:04:22.695 --> 00:04:24.363
I see what it did
to Rob's blade.

00:04:24.930 --> 00:04:28.568
My sword has got to hold up
four swings, and I know J.,

00:04:28.601 --> 00:04:30.470
he's going
to try to do some damage.

00:04:51.057 --> 00:04:54.760
Jared, your blade survived.
Robert, unfortunately,

00:04:54.793 --> 00:04:57.096
your blade cannot continue to be
tested in this competition,

00:04:57.163 --> 00:04:58.564
and for that reason,

00:04:58.631 --> 00:05:00.533
I have to ask you
to please leave the forge.

00:05:00.566 --> 00:05:03.169
Come on forward, my friend.
You killed the Medusa though.

00:05:03.936 --> 00:05:06.973 size:88% position:44%
It's a heartbreaker, but I'm
really proud of what I did.

00:05:09.942 --> 00:05:13.746
Jared, congratulations.
The strength of your weapon

00:05:13.813 --> 00:05:16.682
has ensured that you are
the "Forged in Fire" champion

00:05:16.716 --> 00:05:19.619
leaving this forge with a check
for $10,000. Good job, brother.

00:05:19.685 --> 00:05:21.387
Awesome. Thank you. Thank you.

00:05:23.456 --> 00:05:25.191
-How you feeling right now?
-Good.

00:05:25.224 --> 00:05:26.926
-How about a smile or something?
-Yeah.

00:05:27.793 --> 00:05:29.762
All right. Come on over
and shake our hands, brother.

00:05:29.829 --> 00:05:31.664
-Thank you.
-Good job, man. Good game.

00:05:32.398 --> 00:05:34.467
I am the new "Forged in Fire"
champion,

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:36.469
something
I never thought I'd say.

00:05:36.536 --> 00:05:38.871
I can't wait to get home,
give my daughters the news

00:05:38.904 --> 00:05:40.906
and take the $10,000,

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:42.875
take my family on a vacation
somewhere.

